      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a very common and necessary critique of the era's literature, and you should absolutely address it head-on. The dehumanizing portrayals of African characters are a direct reflection of the racist ideologies prevalent during the height of European imperialism. You can frame this as a critical lens through which students must analyze the text's inherent biases, rather than accepting them as objective truth. This allows the course to move beyond simply reading the book to actively deconstructing its problematic foundations.",
      "source": "target",
