      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea of \"historical accuracy\" in literature is a rich, but often complicated, debate. While you can certainly note that the language reflects the period's prevailing thought, simply labeling it \"accurate\" risks excusing the inherent prejudice. The goal of a post-colonial course isn't just to document history; it's to critique it. You can state that the text *reflects* the period's worldview while simultaneously inviting students to *judge* that worldview by modern ethical standards.",
